  "lineage": "Rural dance-song of Santiago del Estero and the Argentine northwest, documented from the 1880s and codified for the concert stage by Andrés Chazarreta's 1911 Salta company and later Los Hermanos Ábalos and the Carabajal clan, built on a fast 6/8-against-3/4 hemiola strummed on nylon guitar with a rasguido that accents the sesquialtera, driven by bombo legüero played alternately on parche and aro, sung in strophic coplas of eight-bar periods with the doble variant extending each section to sixteen.",
